							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">they were talking about this on Hip Hop vs. America yesterday. The rappers were arguing that the life on the streets is supposed to be heard by people with similar lives. But 90% of these records that have repetitive songs and lyrics about the &quot;hustle&quot; are being sold to white kids in the suburbs that shouldnt have a connection to the music.<br />I am a white kid who lives in the suburbs but i don&#039;t buy that crap cause <br />1) it has no connection to me <br />2) the emcees arn&#039;t very talanted; and<br />3) i dont want to support them so music like this doesn&#039;t get keep getting popularized<br /><br />if these kids in the suburbs keep buying it, people are going to keep making it...</div>
